stone to the north, flat and three storeys with tall narrow windows; the courtyard behind. Placement and footprint from the OpenStreetMap ground; description from DC preservation records (HPRB staff report, DC Historic Sites). No photographs were available: roof pitch, window rhythm, the wing's exact size and the annex's height were guessed. Refined 25 Sep 2026 (still without photographs): a regular window rhythm was added across the main house's south and west brick faces, which had been reading as blank walls; a curved double stair and rounded two-storey entrance portico added on 21st Street, the building's documented and most recognisable feature, which the first pass omitted; tall narrow windows added to the Sant Building and the Main Gallery wing's plain stone faces, matching their published description."}